This directory holds the project's private libraries, each registered as an
ESP-IDF component.

Each library lives in its own directory ("lib/<YourLibrary>/") and contains a
CMakeLists.txt that calls idf_component_register(). The top-level project picks
them up via EXTRA_COMPONENT_DIRS in idf/CMakeLists.txt.

Typical layout:

    |--lib
    |  |
    |  |--Gantry
    |  |  |--src
    |  |  |   |- Gantry.cpp
    |  |  |   |- Gantry.h
    |  |  |- CMakeLists.txt   (idf_component_register: SRCS / INCLUDE_DIRS / REQUIRES)
    |  |
    |  |--EtherNetIP
    |  |  |--src
    |  |  |- CMakeLists.txt
    |  |
    |  |--W5500
    |  |  |--src
    |  |  |- CMakeLists.txt
    |  |
    |- README --> THIS FILE

A component exposes its public headers via INCLUDE_DIRS and declares its
dependencies via REQUIRES. Consumers add the component name to their own
REQUIRES list to link against it.

Build the whole project from the repo root:
  idf.py -C idf build

See CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/LOW_LEVEL_GANTRY_CONTROL.md for build/flash workflow.
